    "name": "Hyperbolic entailment cones",
    "description": "The text introduces a novel method for embedding directed acyclic graphs (DAGs). This model advocates for using hyperbolic spaces because they provably model tree-like structures better than Euclidean geometry. Furthermore, it views hierarchical relations as partial orders defined by a family of nested geodesically convex cones. The approach proves that these entailment cones admit an optimal shape with a closed form expression in both Euclidean and hyperbolic spaces, which canonically defines the embedding learning process. Experiments demonstrate significant improvements over recent baselines in terms of representational capacity and generalization.",
